## Automated Path Format Validation

For more efficient path format validation, the following tool sequence can be used:

```typescript
// 1. Extract all reference paths
grep_search("@[a-z0-9-/]+\\.[a-z]+", false, "1000xbrain/**/*.md")

// 2. Check for non-standard paths
grep_search("@(?!parameters/rules/)[^\\s]+\\.mdc", false, "1000xbrain/**/*.md")

// 3. Check directory structure alignment
list_dir("1000xbrain/parameters/rules")

// 4. Check for unusual capitalization or separators
grep_search("@[A-Z]|@parameters\\\\rules", false, "1000xbrain/**/*.md")

// 5. Document validation results
edit_file("1000xbrain/workflows/rules-workflow/path-validation-results.md", 
          "Document path format validation results",
          "# Path Format Validation Results\n\n...")
```

This path format validation process ensures consistent path references throughout the 1000xbrain cognitive architecture, providing clear and unambiguous file locations and preventing reference errors. 